.TH "STYLEPROPERTYMAPREADONLY.GET" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
StylePropertyMapReadOnly.get \- StylePropertyMapReadOnly: get() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]get()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly\f[R] interface returns a
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue\f[R]\-derived object for the first value of the
specified property.
.PP
Use \f[CR]getAll()\f[R] to get all the values of a CSS property that can
have multiple values, such as \f[CR]background\-image\f[R] or
\f[CR]transition\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
get(property)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]property\f[R]
The name of the property.
Custom property names (starting with \f[CR]\-\-\f[R]) are matched
case\-sensitively; standard property names are not.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSStyleValue\f[R]\-derived object, or \f[CR]undefined\f[R] if
\f[CR]property\f[R] has no value in the map.
.PP
The concrete type of the returned object depends on the property and its
value.
For example, a property assigned a keyword might return a
\f[CR]CSSKeywordValue\f[R], while a property assigned the result of a
mathematical operation might return a \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]property\f[R] is not a valid CSS property name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example shows how to get a few properties and their values.
.SS HTML
First we create a link inside a paragraph:
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]p\f[R]>
  <\f[B]a\f[R] href=\(dqhttps://example.com\(dq>Link</\f[B]a\f[R]>
</\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
The CSS styles the \f[CR]font\-weight\f[R] of the paragraph, and defines
and uses a custom property for the color of the link:
.IP
.EX
p {
  \f[B]font\-weight\f[R]: bold;
}
a {
  \-\-color: red;
  \f[B]color\f[R]: var(\-\-color);
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
First we call \f[CR]computedStyleMap()\f[R] on the element to get its
style map: a \f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly\f[R] object.
We create an array of properties of interest and use the
\f[CR]get()\f[R] method of \f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly\f[R] to log
only those values.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// get the element and its style map\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] myElement = document.querySelector(\(dqa\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = myElement.computedStyleMap();

\f[I]// array of properties we\(aqre interested in\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] properties = [\(dqfont\-weight\(dq, \(dqborder\-left\-color\(dq, \(dqcolor\(dq, \(dq\-\-color\(dq];

\f[I]// log the value of each property of interest\f[R]
\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] property \f[B]of\f[R] properties) {
  log(\(ga${property}: ${styleMap.get(property)}\(ga);
}
.EE
.SS Result
.SS Getting different value types
This example demonstrates that \f[CR]get()\f[R] can return objects of
different types, depending on the property and its value.
.PP
First it applies a number of different properties to an element using
CSS.
It then reads them back via JavaScript and logs the constructor name and
value of each property.
The logging code itself isn\(cqt part of the demonstration, so it\(cqs
hidden here.
.SS HTML
First we define an \f[CR]<div>\f[R] with id \f[CR]demoBox\f[R] to which
we\(cqll add styles.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqdemoBox\(dq>Text</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
demoBox {
  \-\-my\-custom\-property: \(dqsome text\(dq;
  \f[B]opacity\f[R]: 0.5;
  \f[B]width\f[R]: calc(30% \- 20px);
  \f[B]display\f[R]: block;
  \f[B]transform\f[R]: translate(10px, 10px);
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
Next we use \f[CR]computedStyleMap()\f[R] to get the
\f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly\f[R] object for the demo box, and iterate
through each of the properties we added, logging their constructor name
and value.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = document.querySelector(\(dq#demoBox\(dq).computedStyleMap();
\f[B]const\f[R] properties = [
  \(dqopacity\(dq,
  \(dqdisplay\(dq,
  \(dqwidth\(dq,
  \(dqtransform\(dq,
  \(dq\-\-my\-custom\-property\(dq,
];

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] property \f[B]of\f[R] properties) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] value = styleMap.get(property);
  log(property);
  log(\(ga  type: ${value.constructor.name}\(ga);
  log(\(ga  value: ${value}\(rsn\(ga);
}
.EE
.SS Result
